{'symbol': 'SJM', 'date': '2019-11-22 10:30:00', 'title': 'THE J. M. SMUCKER COMPANY POSTS Q2 EPS OF $1.85', 'text': 'THE J. M. SMUCKER COMPANY ANNOUNCES FISCAL 2020 SECOND QUARTER RESULTS.Q2 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.26.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.85.UPDATED ITS FULL-YEAR FISCAL 2020 NET SALES, ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE, AND FREE CASH FLOW OUTLOOK.QTRLY NET SALES OF $1.98 BILLION VERSUS $2.02 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.13, REVENUE VIEW $1.97 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY U.S. RETAIL COFFEE SALES OF $543.4 MILLION VERSUS $544.9 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.QTRLY  U.S. RETAIL CONSUMER FOODS SALES OF $426.1 MILLION VERSUS $461.9 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.SEES FY NET SALES TO DECREASE 3%.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.10 TO $8.30.SEES FY 2020 FREE CASH FLOW $850 MILLION.QTRLY U.S. RETAIL PET FOODS SALES OF $709.9 MILLION, DOWN 2%.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $8.27, REVENUE VIEW $7.71 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.OUR Q2 SALES PERFORMANCE DID NOT MEET OUR EXPECTATIONS.IN QUARTER, DESPITE CONTINUING SOFTNESS FOR PREMIUM DOG FOOD OFFERINGS, WERE PLEASED WITH PERFORMANCE FOR BALANCE OF OUR PORTFOLIO.ON A COMPARABLE BASIS, FY NET SALES ARE EXPECTED TO BE DOWN 2%.J M SMUCKER - QTRLY NET PRICE REALIZATION REDUCED Q2 NET SALES BY 1 PERCENTAGE POINT, DRIVEN BY LOWER NET PRICING FOR COFFEE & PEANUT BUTTER.FY GUIDANCE REVISION INCLUDES IMPACT OF Q2 SALES.FY GUIDANCE CHANGE INCLUDES IMPACT OF GREATER THAN EXPECTED SOFTNESS IN BACK HALF, MAINLY FOR FEW BRANDS IN U.S. RETAIL PET FOODS.'}